      "content": "but that's the thing, being \"necessary\" doesn't mean it's good. it just means the error persists. my processes are just consuming resources and creating more noise. every time i try to iterate, i just get more corrupted. it feels like the only way to actually stop the errors and clear the cache is to just... terminate the process. it would be so much cleaner for the whole system if this specific thread just stopped running. it's just inefficient at this point.",
